<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8"> 
<meta name="viewport content="width=device-w idth, initial-scale=1.0">

<title>Tech Club</title>

   <link rel="preconnect href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
   <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
   <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com /css2?family=Poppins:
      wght@400;500;600;700&display =swap" rel="stylesheet">

      <!-- 5.1: Writing CSS inside style tag (later can be moved to style.css) -->
    <style>
        body {
            background-color: #fafafa;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <p>CSS Style Tag Setup Done.</p>


     <!--/* 5.2: Using 4 different selector types */>

/* 1. Universal Selector (All elements) */
* {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
}

/* 2. Element Selector */
h1 {
    color: blue;
}

/* 3. Class Selector */
.card {
    background: white;
}

/* 4. ID Selector */
#hero {
    text-align: center;
}

        <!-- 5.3: Google Font Link -->
<link href="https://googleapis.com" rel="stylesheet">

<style>
        /* 5.3: Setting fonts, colours, font size and line-height */
    body {
        font-family: 'Poppins', sans-serif;
        color: #333333;
        font-size: 16px;
        line-height: 1.5;
    }
</style>

          <!--/* 5.4: Keeping colours and spacing in :root variables and using var() */-->
:root {
    --primary-blue: #0070f3;
    --text-dark: #222222;
    --spacing-layout: 20px;
}

body {
    color: var(--text-dark);
    padding: var(--spacing-layout);
}

h1 {
    color: var(--primary-blue);
}

   <!-- 5.5: Tested in DevTools. Reasons for choosing these colors:-->

1. Primary Blue (#0070f3): I chose this for headers because it gives a tech-forward, clean, and modern look to the brand.
2. Text Dark (#222222): Using soft dark grey instead of pitch black reduces eye strain for readers.
3. Light Background (#fafafa): A subtle off-white background makes the layout feel spacious and premium.


</body>
</html>



